    {
      "kind": "statement",
      "eyebrow": "01 · The thesis",
      "title": "The technology is not the story. The cost line is.",
      "body": "Utilities earn a regulated return on capital. The technology story is a demand story: data centres and electrification turn a low-growth sector into a capacity-build sector. Whoever can add firm, clean generation and interconnect it fastest earns a growing rate base; whoever cannot faces cost inflation and stranded assets."
    },
    {
      "kind": "points",
      "eyebrow": "02 · Sector economics",
      "title": "What this sector actually sells",
      "body": "Revenue is rate base times allowed return, plus pass-through fuel cost. Load growth, capex and allowed ROE drive earnings; weather and outages drive variance.",
      "bullets": [
        "Regulated returns are set on rate base, so capex growth is earnings growth if allowed.",
        "Load growth has been near zero for a decade; data centres change that.",
        "Fuel and purchased power are largely pass-through, but lag and hedging create risk.",
        "Grid capex is rising faster than sales, pressuring customer bills.",
        "Merchant generators earn on spark spreads and capacity prices."
      ]
    },
